$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure 2: Oxidation of the alcohols to the aldehydes 1-4. The
alcohol S4 a-d (1.0 eq.) was dissolved in DMSO (10mL/mmol) and
2-iodoxybenzoic acid (IBX, 1.5 eq.) was added. After stirring for 12h at
rt, the mixture was added to DCM and washed with dem. water (3x),
saturated NaHCO3 (aq) (3x) and brine (2x). Evaporation gives the
corresponding aldehyde without the need for further purification.
(3S)-tert-Butyl
3-((S)-2-(((benzyloxy)carbonyl)amino)-4-methylpentanamido)-4-
oxo-4-((1-oxopropan-2-yl)amino)butanoate (2). General procedure 2; yield:
100.0%, colorless oil, mixture of diasteromers. 1H-NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3,
300 K): δ [ppm] = 9.42 (1H, s), 7.52 (1NH, m), 7.30 (5H, m), 5.56 (1NH,
m), 5.02 (2H, m), 4.81 (1H, m), 4.27 (1H, m), 4.09 (1H, m), 2.77 (2H, m),
1.66 (2H, m), 1.52 (1H, m), 1.42 (9H, s), 1.27 (3H, m), 0.92 (6H, m).
13C-NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3, 300 K): δ [ppm] = 200.08, 172.68, 171.43,
170.93, 156.99, 136.26, 128.85, 128.55, 128.21, 82.16, 67.52, 54.85,
54.69, 49.49, 40.94, 36.81, 28.26, 25.04, 23.00, 22.10, 14.21. HPLC: tR =
6.11 min. ESI-MS: m/z = 514.
