$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (3aR,4R,6S,6aS)-4-(2,4-dioxo-3,4-dihydropyrimidin-1(2H)-yl)-6-formyl-2,2-dimethyltetrahydrofuro[3,4-d][1,3]dioxole-4-carbonitrile
(8): 2-Iodoxybenzoic acid (IBX) (3 g, 4.8 mmol, 45% wt) was stirred with
EtOAc (15 mL) for 15 minutes until a homogeneous mixture formed. The
solid was isolated by suction filtration and then added to a solution of
the starting material (500 mg, 1.6 mmol) in CH3CN (20 mL). The mixture
was heated at 80°C for 30 minutes. The reaction mixture was cooled in an
ice bath and the mother liquor was isolated by suction filtration. The
solvent was removed under reduced pressure, and the white solid was
azeotroped with toluene. The aldehyde 8 was used immediately, and the
yield was assumed to be 100%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of 1'-C-Cyano Pyrimidine Nucleosides and Characterization as
HCV Polymerase Inhibitors
