$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a solution of tetraol 29 (15.5 mg, 25.7 μmol) in DMSO (2.0 mL) was
added IBX (21.0 mg, 75.0 μmol) at room temperature. After stirring for 2
h, the reaction mixture was poured into 10% Na2S2O3 aq. at 0 ºC. The
products were extracted with CH2Cl2, and the combined organic extracts
were washed with water, brine, dried over Na2SO4, filtered and
concentrated. The residue was purified by preparative thin-layer
chromatography (CHCl3/MeOH = 95/5). Aldehyde 30 (14.4 mg, 93%) as yellow
solids. Reprecipitation from hexane/CH2Cl2 gave 30 as yellow powders. R f
0.38 (CHCl3/MeOH = 95/5); Mp 154-156 ºC; [α]D 25 +86 (c 1.0, CHCl3); 1H
NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 1.15 (s, 3H), 2.42 (dd, 1H, J = 16.1, 2.2 Hz),
2.48 (s, 3H), 2.58 (dd, 1H, J = 16.1, 2.2 Hz), 2.77 (d, 1H, J = 13.9 Hz),
2.81 (d, 1H, J = 13.9 Hz), 3.73 (s, 1H, OH), 3.94 (s, 6H), 3.98 (s, 3H),
6.77 (d, 1H, J = 2.3 Hz), 7.11 (s, 1H), 7.35 (d, 1H, J = 2.3 Hz), 7.49
(s, 1H), 7.67 (s, 1H), 9.73 (dd, 1H, J 1 = J 2 = 2.2 Hz), 12.0 (s, 1H,
OH), 12.4 (s, 1H, OH); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 22.2, 27.9, 40.8, 54.7,
56.0, 56.4, 56.6, 72.0, 103.2, 103.6, 104.5, 110.9, 113.5, 114.4, 117.3,
121.5, 124.7, 132.9, 135.6, 135.9, 143.5, 144.2, 148.8, 160.7, 162.0,
162.6, 163.1, 164.7, 179.9, 181.7, 187.1, 191.1, 202.4; IR (ATR) 3467,
2971, 2945, 2843, 1717, 1657, 1622, 1594, 1563, 1477, 1424, 1407, 1357,
1275, 1230, 1205, 1158, 1133, 1102, 1085, 1069, 998, 971, 920, 872, 830,
762, 724 cm-1; HRMS (ESI-TOF) calcd for C33H29O11 ([M+H]+) m/z 601.1710,
found, 601.1708.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM First Total Synthesis of Dermocanarin 2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
