$DATUM Ketone S7: To a solution of MOM ether S6 (5.5 g, 15.3 mmol) in DMSO (75
mL) was added 2-iodoxybenzoic acid (4.7 g, 16.8 mmol) at RT, and the
mixture was heated at 50 °C. After stirring for 1 h, the reaction was
quenched by addition of H2O, and extracted with ethyl acetate. The
organic layer was washed with H2O and brine, dried over MgSO4, and
concentrated in vacuo. The residue was purified by column chromatography
on SiO2 (ethyl acetate/hexane 1:2 to 1:1). Ketone S7 (4.95g, 91%) as a
pale yellow oil. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.61 (d, J = 7.3 Hz, 2H),
7.39-7.28 (m, 3H), 7.06 (d, J = 8.2 Hz, 1H), 6.97 (d, J = 8.2 Hz, 1H),
5.04 (s, 2H), 4.63 (s, 2H), 3.85 (s, 3H), 3.54-3.47 (m, 2H), 3.67 (s,
3H), 2.98 (d, J = 15.5 Hz, 1H), 2.77-2.68 (m, 2H), 2.47-2.37 (m, 2H); 13C
NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 196.86, 152.38, 148.15, 137.59, 135.87, 128.75,
128.17, 127.80, 127.38, 124.28, 117.53, 96.46, 74.98, 70.76, 56.36,
55.19, 43.53, 35.42, 32.93; HRMS (ESI, M+Na) calcd for C21H24NaO5
379.1521, found 379.1565.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Origin of Stereocontrol in Guanidine-Bisurea Bifunctional Organocatalyst
That Promotes α-Hydroxylation of Tetralone-Derived β-Ketoesters:
